#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 51
#: rc.cpp:688
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generate Rock Ridge extensions"
msgstr "\"Rock Ridge\"-Verwiedern opstellen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 57
#: rc.cpp:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Rock Ridge extensions to the file system"
msgstr "\"Rock Ridge\"-Verwiedern to de Dateisysteem tofögen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 63
#: rc.cpp:694
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will generate the System Use Sharing Protocol "
"records (SUSP) specified by the Rock Ridge Interchange Protocol (IEEE-P1282).\n"
"<p>Rock Ridge extends the ISO-9660 filesystem by features equal to the UNIX "
"filesystems (permissions, symbolic links, very long filenames, ...). It uses "
"ISO-8859 or UTF-16 based characters and allows 255 octets.\n"
"<p>Rock Ridge extensions are located at the end of each ISO-9660 directory "
"record. This makes the Rock Ridge tree closely coupled to the ISO-9660 tree.\n"
"<p><b>It is highly recommended to use Rock Ridge extensions on every data CD or "
"DVD.</b>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon aktiveert is, warrt K3b de \"Systeem bruukt "
"Freegaavprotokoll-Indrääg\" (\"System Use Sharing Protocol\", SUSP), welk in'n "
"Rock-Ridge Kommunikatschoonprotokoll (IEEE-P1282) angeven sünd, opstellen.\n"
"<p>Rock-Ridge verwiedert dat ISO9660-Dateisysteem mit Markmalen vun de "
"UNIX-Dateisystemen (Verlöven, symboolsch Links, bannig lang Dateinaams, ...). "
"Dat bruukt ISO-8859- oder UTF-16-baseert Tekens, un lett 255-Oktetten to.\n"
"<p>De Rock-Ridge-Verwiedern liggt an'n Enn vun elk ISO-9660 Ornerindrag. Dat "
"koppelt jem drang mit den ISO-9660-Boom tosamen.\n"
"<p><b>Dat is redig anraadt, dat Du de Rock-Ridge-Verwiedern för elk Daten-CD "
"oder -DVD bruukst.</b>"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 71
#: rc.cpp:700
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generate Joliet extensions"
msgstr "\"Joliet\"-Verwiedern opstellen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 74
#: rc.cpp:703
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Joliet extensions to the file system"
msgstr "\"Joliet\"-Verwiedern to de Dateisysteem tofögen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 81
#: rc.cpp:706
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will add additional Joliet extensions to the "
"ISO-9660 file system.\n"
"<p>Joliet is not an accepted independent international standard like ISO-9660 "
"or Rock Ridge. It is mainly used on Windows systems.\n"
"<p>Joliet does not allow all characters, so the Joliet filenames are not "
"identical to the filenames on disk (as compared to Rock Ridge). Joliet has a "
"filename length limitation of 64 chars (independent from the character coding "
"and type e.g. European vs. Japanese). This is annoying, as modern file systems "
"all allow 255 characters per path name component.\n"
"<p>Joliet uses UTF-16 coding.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> With the exception of Linux and FreeBSD, there is no "
"POSIX-like OS that supports Joliet. So <b>never create Joliet-only CDs or "
"DVDs</b> for that reason."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon aktiveert is, warrt K3b bito noch Joliet-Verwiedern "
"na't ISO-9660 Dateisysteem tofögen.\n"
"<p>Joliet is keen tolaten, nich afhangig internatschonaal Standard, as ISO-9660 "
"oder Rock-Ridge dat sünd. Dat warrt tomehrst op Windowssystemen bruukt.\n"
"<p>Joliet verlöövt nich all Tekens. De Joliet-Dateinaams sünd nich de sülven "
"Dateinaams, as op de Schiev. (vergleken mit Rock-Ridge.) Joliet hett en Grenz "
"för de Dateinaams vun 64 Tekens. (Egaal, welk Tekensett un Typ, t.B. europääsch "
"oder japaansch). Dat is verdreetlich, wiel all modern Dateisysteemen 255 Tekens "
"per Paddnaam verlöövt.\n"
"<p>Joliet bruukt UTF-16-Koderen.\n"
"<p><b>Wohrscho:</b> Afsehn vun Linux un FreeBSD gifft dat keen POSIX-liek "
"Bedriefsysteem, dat Joliet ünnerstütt. So is dat anraadt, wat Du <b>"
"nienich keen \"bloots-Joliet\"-CD oder -DVD opstellst</b>."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 89
#: rc.cpp:713
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generate UDF structures"
msgstr "UDF-Strukturen warrt opstellt"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 92
#: rc.cpp:716
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add UDF structures to the file system"
msgstr "UDF-Strukturen na Dateisysteem tofögen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 96
#: rc.cpp:719
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked K3b will create UDF filesystem structures in "
"addition to the ISO9660 filesystem.\n"
"<p>The UDF (<em><b>U</b>niversal <b>D</b>isk <b>F</b>ormat</em>"
") is mainly used for DVDs."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon aktiveert is, warrt K3b UDF-Dateisysteemstrukturen "
"tosamen mit de ISO9660-Dateisysteem opstellen.\n"
"<p>Dat UDF (<em><b>U</b>niversal <b>D</b>isk <b>F</b>ormaat</em>"
") warrt tomehrst för DVDs bruukt."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 106
#: rc.cpp:723
#, no-c-format
msgid "Symbolic Links"
msgstr "Symboolsch Links"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 123
#: rc.cpp:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "Discard all symlinks"
msgstr "All Symlinks wegsmieten"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 126
#: rc.cpp:729
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do not create symbolic links"
msgstr "Keen Symlinks opstellen"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 130
#: rc.cpp:732
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will ignore all symbolic links that have been "
"added to the project; meaning that the resulting file system will have no links "
"at all.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> Symbolic links require Rock Ridge extensions."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon utwählt is, övergaht K3b all Symlinks in de Projekt, "
"wat bedüüdt, dat dat opstellt Systeem gor keen Links hett.\n"
"<p><b>Wohrscho:</b> Symlinks bruukt \"Rock-Ridge\"-Verwiedern."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 146
#: rc.cpp:736
#, no-c-format
msgid "Discard broken symlinks"
msgstr "Leeg Symlinks wegsmieten"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 149
#: rc.cpp:739
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore all links pointing outside the project"
msgstr "Smitt all symboolsch Links weg, wat vun de Projekt na buten wiest."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 153
#: rc.cpp:742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will discard all symbolic links that do not "
"point to a file inside the project. That includes all links to absolute paths "
"like '/home/myhome/testfile'.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> Symbolic links require Rock Ridge extensions."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon utwählt is, warrt K3b all Symlinks wegsmieten, wat nich "
"na en Datei in 't Projekt wiest. Dat meent denn ok all afsoluut Symlinks as "
"\"/home/tohuus/testdatei\"."
"<p><b>Wohrscho:</b> Symlinks bruukt de \"Rock-Ridge\"-Verwiedern."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 161
#: rc.cpp:746
#, no-c-format
msgid "Follow symbolic links"
msgstr "Symboolsch Links nagahn"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 164
#: rc.cpp:749
#, no-c-format
msgid "Follow symbolic links for source files"
msgstr "Symboolsch Links för Borndateien nagahn"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 168
#: rc.cpp:752
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked every symbolic link in the project will be "
"replaced with the contents of the file it is pointing to. This means that the "
"resulting filesystem will not contain any symbolic links.\n"
"<p>Be aware that in case Rock Ridge extensions are disabled (which is not "
"recommended) symbolic links are always followed because ISO9660 does not "
"support symbolic links."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon utwählt is, warrt elk Symlink in 't Projekt dör de "
"Teel-Dateiinholt utwesselt. So warrt in de Teel-Dateisysteem keen Symlink "
"binnen wesen.\n"
"<p>Beacht, dat mit utmaakt \"Rock-Ridge\"-Verwiedern (wat nich anraadt is) "
"Symlinks jümmers nagahn warrt, wiel ISO9660 Symlinks nich ünnerstütt."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 178
#: rc.cpp:756
#, no-c-format
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr "Verlöven"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 195
#: rc.cpp:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preserve file permissions (backup)"
msgstr "Dateiverlöven wohren (Sekerheitskopie)"

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 199
#: rc.cpp:762
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, all files in the resulting file system will have "
"exactly the same permissions as the source files. (Otherwise, all files will "
"have equal permissions and be owned by root).\n"
"<p>This is mainly useful for backups."
"<p><b>Caution:</b> The permissions may not make much sense on other file "
"systems; for example, if a user that owns a file on the CD or DVD does not "
"exist."
msgstr ""
"<p>Wenn disse Optschoon aktiveert is, hebbt all Dateien in de Teeldateisysteem "
"akraat de sülven Verlöven as de Borndatei. (Anners hebbt all Dateien de sülven "
"Verlöven, un höört to \"root\").\n"
"<p>Dat is för Sekerheitskopien sinnvull."
"<p><b>Wohrscho:</b>De Verlöven sünd op anner Dateisystemen nich jümmers "
"sinnvull, t.B., wenn dat den Bruker vun de Datei nich gifft."

#. i18n: file ./projects/base_k3bdataimagesettings.ui line 217
#: rc.cpp:766
#, no-c-format
